WEBVTT

00:00:05.220 --> 00:00:08.020
Yeah, I think I've also heard of it.

00:00:08.400 --> 00:00:11.400
What could those "Yami" and "Yomi" be?

00:00:11.920 --> 00:00:13.000
I don't know.

00:00:13.480 --> 00:00:16.340
But, the only thing that we're sure of is that,

00:00:16.660 --> 00:00:20.220
there is an increase in the number of dangerous people gathering around you.

00:00:20.660 --> 00:00:21.420
<i>Me?</i>

00:00:21.420 --> 00:00:22.480
Why me?!

00:00:23.740 --> 00:00:26.600
Grandpa and the others seem to know something,

00:00:26.600 --> 00:00:28.980
but in order not to worry you too much

00:00:28.980 --> 00:00:31.400
they seem to be hiding it.

00:00:31.720 --> 00:00:34.080
I'm already getting worried by the fact that <i>it's</i>  being hidden.

00:00:34.560 --> 00:00:35.540
Hey Ken-chan.

00:00:35.540 --> 00:00:38.100
You'll lose your balance if you veer away too much.

00:00:41.950 --> 00:00:42.590
Oh no.

00:00:44.030 --> 00:00:45.280
Pervert.

00:00:50.480 --> 00:00:51.360
But,

00:00:51.660 --> 00:00:54.680
the fact that we even won twice when challenged

00:00:54.980 --> 00:00:57.800
is vastly thanks to my training at Ryouzanpaku.

00:00:58.420 --> 00:01:01.860
I'm far different from the person that I was when I was still bullied.

00:01:03.020 --> 00:01:04.140
That's right.

00:01:05.940 --> 00:01:09.500
I wonder how strong I really am now.

00:01:12.720 --> 00:01:16.680
So Kenichi-kun is already at that age where he thinks about that~

00:01:16.680 --> 00:01:18.860
No, I don't think age has anything to do with it.

00:01:19.320 --> 00:01:21.350
There are a lot of ways to find out~

00:01:21.400 --> 00:01:23.010
There's the dangerous way,

00:01:23.080 --> 00:01:27.180
and then the comparably more dangerous way~

00:01:25.700 --> 00:01:27.180
<i>Give me the safe way instead, please.</i>

00:01:27.880 --> 00:01:30.640
Oh, but if it's the safe one~

00:01:30.830 --> 00:01:34.420
One method is to look at your many battles~

00:01:34.430 --> 00:01:37.160
And compare yourself to each one of them~

00:01:37.640 --> 00:01:39.240
But even still in the end~

00:01:39.970 --> 00:01:42.820
You'll have to push yourself to your utmost limit,

00:01:42.820 --> 00:01:45.580
make a deal with your life at death's land,

00:01:45.580 --> 00:01:49.380
catch a glimpse of light and darkness at the ravines of the holy land~!

00:01:49.380 --> 00:01:51.260
<i>I am grateful for your consultation!</i>

00:01:58.720 --> 00:02:00.560
What are you two doing?

00:02:01.500 --> 00:02:02.920
Shh!

00:02:04.420 --> 00:02:07.930
Then, I'll leave it to you to report it to the other side, Sakaki-kun.

00:02:13.520 --> 00:02:15.920
Who were those people?

00:02:16.820 --> 00:02:17.970
Oh, they are detectives.

00:02:18.600 --> 00:02:19.460
Detectives?

00:02:19.860 --> 00:02:20.800
Investigators?

00:02:21.340 --> 00:02:22.440
<i>You mean the police?!</i>

00:02:22.520 --> 00:02:24.600
Wh-what the hell did you do?!

00:02:24.600 --> 00:02:25.360
Surrender yourself.

00:02:25.360 --> 00:02:25.780
Surrender...

00:02:25.780 --> 00:02:26.400
Surrender...

00:02:26.480 --> 00:02:27.800
Y-you fool!

00:02:27.800 --> 00:02:29.040
I didn't do anything!

00:02:29.280 --> 00:02:31.280
Then what was the police...

00:02:32.760 --> 00:02:33.640
They asked for a request.

00:02:33.760 --> 00:02:34.840
It's work.

00:02:35.560 --> 00:02:36.780
Work?

00:02:36.780 --> 00:02:38.960
I go out into the field sometimes.

00:02:39.220 --> 00:02:43.640
These are external and dangerous jobs that cannot be done by normal people.

00:02:45.560 --> 00:02:46.580
That's it!

00:02:46.800 --> 00:02:48.130
This might be perfect.

00:02:55.480 --> 00:02:56.860
Gorgeous!

00:02:57.120 --> 00:02:58.580
A Hollywood star maybe?

00:03:05.280 --> 00:03:07.620
What a filthy country.

00:03:08.160 --> 00:03:10.900
Are the pre-preparations finished?

00:03:11.300 --> 00:03:12.710
Yes, Professor.

00:03:13.910 --> 00:03:17.910
Ken

00:03:13.910 --> 00:03:17.910
Su

00:03:14.430 --> 00:03:17.910
b

00:03:14.450 --> 00:03:17.910
i

00:03:14.990 --> 00:03:17.910
ch

00:03:14.990 --> 00:03:17.910
DE

00:03:15.550 --> 00:03:17.910
i

00:03:15.550 --> 00:03:17.910
SU

00:03:18.080 --> 00:03:25.380
Kenichi

00:03:18.080 --> 00:03:25.380
SubDESU

00:03:18.580 --> 00:03:25.380
History's Strongest Disciple

00:03:18.580 --> 00:03:25.380
Presents

00:03:25.710 --> 00:03:29.300
The gorgeous assassin

00:03:27.780 --> 00:03:29.310
Observation of the Underworld Community?

00:03:29.980 --> 00:03:33.640
What's with that clearly suspicious job?

00:03:35.180 --> 00:03:37.860
You don't have to be that jumpy, Kenichi-kun.

00:03:37.980 --> 00:03:39.200
That's right.

00:03:39.200 --> 00:03:40.350
All of us here agree that

00:03:40.460 --> 00:03:46.280
it'll be a good chance for you to observe the martial arts world.

00:03:46.560 --> 00:03:48.960
Some unseen problem will most likely pop up though,

00:03:48.960 --> 00:03:51.280
so I'm not too sure about this.

00:03:51.280 --> 00:03:54.110
You think too hard, Sakaki-don.

00:03:54.400 --> 00:03:58.640
Well, it's for the best that you experience it this early.

00:03:59.210 --> 00:04:00.400
What do you mean?

00:04:00.860 --> 00:04:02.300
But, in anycase,

00:04:02.300 --> 00:04:04.340
regardless of time,

00:04:04.340 --> 00:04:07.840
this will totally immerse Ken-chan into our world.

00:04:08.120 --> 00:04:09.900
You just said something about me there!

00:04:10.140 --> 00:04:14.180
Martial artists are meant to die fighting anyway.

00:04:14.180 --> 00:04:14.880
Right?

00:04:15.960 --> 00:04:17.880
Harakiri! Sukiyaki!

00:04:15.960 --> 00:04:17.880
TLc Note: Play on words. Harakiri = Stomach cutting / Sukiyaki = Hot pot

00:04:17.400 --> 00:04:18.350
<i>Dangerous people...?</i>

00:04:18.940 --> 00:04:21.080
Die, fighting?

00:04:23.860 --> 00:04:26.320
What's going to happen?!

00:04:26.880 --> 00:04:28.180
Well, we're off then.

00:04:28.440 --> 00:04:29.740
Be careful, okay?

00:04:31.060 --> 00:04:33.140
Where are we...!

00:04:33.140 --> 00:04:36.080
Ke-Kenichi-san, please be safe.

00:04:37.440 --> 00:04:38.500
I see.

00:04:38.500 --> 00:04:42.320
Your job here is something like a bodyguard, right?

00:04:42.320 --> 00:04:43.980
I understand now.

00:04:43.980 --> 00:04:45.100
But...

00:04:45.180 --> 00:04:48.600
I think I would like to have my body guarded instead!

00:04:48.840 --> 00:04:51.360
Well, two fighters without a sword...

00:04:51.390 --> 00:04:52.500
That's all we got?

00:04:53.380 --> 00:04:55.880
Anyway, we don't need any help.

00:04:55.930 --> 00:04:58.110
They will be easily beaten by us.

00:04:58.280 --> 00:05:01.040
Let's see what you can do Japanese.

00:05:02.020 --> 00:05:03.620
I don't speak English!

00:05:03.840 --> 00:05:06.700
I just want to tell you all, firstly...

00:05:15.620 --> 00:05:17.760
You should have a second sword!

00:05:18.100 --> 00:05:19.460
The order is reversed.

00:05:19.460 --> 00:05:20.820
You should have said that before you hit them!

00:05:21.020 --> 00:05:21.880
Huh?

00:05:21.880 --> 00:05:24.540
You're not surprised that I just spoke perfect English?

00:05:24.540 --> 00:05:27.100
There are other things I am more surprised about!

00:05:28.800 --> 00:05:31.080
Wonderful, wonderful.

00:05:32.160 --> 00:05:36.140
As expected of the fabled 100-Dan Street Brawler of Karate, Sakaki Shio.

00:05:40.360 --> 00:05:41.860
It's a good mansion, isn't it?

00:05:41.860 --> 00:05:47.370
The Japanese government has been kind enough to keep me in here secretly.

00:05:47.700 --> 00:05:50.340
I'll like a confirmation on the request details.

00:05:51.940 --> 00:05:53.500
It's nothing but simple.

00:05:53.630 --> 00:05:55.780
During my three-day stay here in Japan,

00:05:55.780 --> 00:05:57.660
you'll act as my personal bodyguard.

00:05:58.140 --> 00:06:00.720
I have a lot of enemies in the business you see.

00:06:01.000 --> 00:06:04.480
And the Japanese police can't back me up officially.

00:06:04.600 --> 00:06:08.680
Things will become troublesome if I get killed halfway through my job.

00:06:09.020 --> 00:06:14.820
So, is it true that the killer that's after you is, Christopher?

00:06:15.400 --> 00:06:17.560
It is merely a rumor,

00:06:17.840 --> 00:06:20.700
but I'm worried even if it's just from my subordinates.

00:06:20.930 --> 00:06:22.700
<i>Christopher?</i>

00:06:23.380 --> 00:06:24.380
Gauche-sama.

00:06:24.380 --> 00:06:25.280
It's about time...

00:06:26.100 --> 00:06:27.000
Master Sakaki.

00:06:27.090 --> 00:06:28.520
Your work starts right now.

00:06:28.880 --> 00:06:32.440
Guard Gauche-sama well until we get to the appointed hotel.

00:06:32.780 --> 00:06:34.060
Okay, okay.

00:06:34.060 --> 00:06:36.680
I'll get you there safely without a sweat.

00:06:36.680 --> 00:06:38.960
And what will happen if you let him die, you monkey?

00:06:38.960 --> 00:06:43.180
In exchange, I'll be guarding him using my own methods.

00:06:49.760 --> 00:06:51.480
Huh? Hey, what's what?

00:06:53.920 --> 00:06:55.430
<i>Oh no!</i>

00:07:15.480 --> 00:07:17.080
Christopher Éclair.

00:07:17.380 --> 00:07:18.360
It's him.

00:07:18.360 --> 00:07:19.580
Who in the world is he?

00:07:20.020 --> 00:07:21.860
His fighting technique is the Savate.

00:07:22.460 --> 00:07:26.640
It's a French martial art that has its roots in Ancient Greece's Pankration.

00:07:27.080 --> 00:07:29.580
It has many foot-based techniques.

00:07:30.440 --> 00:07:36.960
Today, there's a French sports-style Box Savate that has no elbow strikes and throws.

00:07:37.540 --> 00:07:42.480
But his is the type that has been perfected for the killing of the opponent.

00:07:42.480 --> 00:07:44.220
The Murderous Savate.

00:07:44.380 --> 00:07:46.620
He's a cruel and merciless martial artist.

00:07:47.180 --> 00:07:51.540
For Master Sakaki to describe an opponent's ability in such a manner...

00:07:51.540 --> 00:07:54.230
I feel like I just witnessed an outrageously powerful monster...

00:07:54.720 --> 00:07:56.580
He mistook the fake for the real car, right?

00:07:57.880 --> 00:07:59.280
As I thought...

00:07:59.280 --> 00:08:02.500
It was right for us to have switched cars at the last moment.

00:08:02.500 --> 00:08:06.440
He allows his women to put on the same perfume as him as well...

00:08:12.400 --> 00:08:14.220
He's catching up crazily fast!

00:08:20.280 --> 00:08:21.720
Shio-chan!

00:08:21.720 --> 00:08:23.060
Long time no see!

00:08:23.190 --> 00:08:25.100
I'm crazily happy to see you.

00:08:25.380 --> 00:08:26.380
Chris...

00:08:26.380 --> 00:08:28.380
I didn't want to see you though.

00:08:30.180 --> 00:08:31.110
Now, now...

00:08:31.150 --> 00:08:32.860
Saying cold things like that...

00:08:32.860 --> 00:08:34.260
When you're actually happy about it.

00:08:35.000 --> 00:08:36.070
Well then,

00:08:36.140 --> 00:08:37.330
judging by the situation,

00:08:37.340 --> 00:08:38.730
I currently have the upper hand, don't I?

00:08:39.080 --> 00:08:43.670
You can't use the full extent of your powers in this cramped space.

00:08:43.960 --> 00:08:47.820
However, with Savate's unparalleled flexibility and accuracy,

00:08:47.990 --> 00:08:51.560
I can still kick and finish off any target properly.

00:08:52.360 --> 00:08:56.910
Besides, your client and disciple are in my hands.

00:08:57.380 --> 00:08:59.760
So, who will you save?

00:09:00.000 --> 00:09:01.440
Save me!

00:09:01.440 --> 00:09:02.920
I-I'll give you money!

00:09:02.920 --> 00:09:05.380
My life's value is heavier!

00:09:09.900 --> 00:09:11.240
Now, Shio!

00:09:30.880 --> 00:09:33.700
Kenichi!

00:09:36.400 --> 00:09:37.640
What are you doing?

00:09:37.640 --> 00:09:39.040
Is the other car still not coming?

00:09:42.220 --> 00:09:43.960
Christopher, is that you?

00:09:44.590 --> 00:09:49.870
Seriously, you're always trying to get in my way, Shio.

00:09:50.210 --> 00:09:53.280
But, I never thought you'd take a disciple...

00:09:53.520 --> 00:09:55.520
People can truly change if they want to.

00:09:56.260 --> 00:09:58.480
Yeah, I let him live.

00:09:58.900 --> 00:10:00.560
Why don’t we conduct a trade?

00:10:01.100 --> 00:10:04.260
You'll have to follow the time and place that I'm going to set.

00:10:08.900 --> 00:10:10.960
I've got your kids!

00:10:11.200 --> 00:10:13.220
Get Miu on the line, Appachai!

00:10:13.220 --> 00:10:15.020
You’re answering the phone call again!

00:10:15.220 --> 00:10:17.720
Just trying to stretch the conversation as long as possible.

00:10:17.880 --> 00:10:19.740
Yes, this is Fuurinji.

00:10:21.560 --> 00:10:23.760
Like I said, he was kidnapped!

00:10:23.760 --> 00:10:28.600
Kenichi won’t be able to return home until I've cleaned up this job.

00:10:29.020 --> 00:10:32.200
Try to cover for him in school or someth– huh?

00:10:32.410 --> 00:10:34.480
I said I'm also coming.

00:10:34.780 --> 00:10:37.280
If something happens to Kenichi-san...

00:10:37.460 --> 00:10:40.420
Anyway, please tell me where the exchange will take place!

00:10:50.160 --> 00:10:51.380
What's wrong?

00:10:51.380 --> 00:10:52.820
Try to eat something.

00:10:52.820 --> 00:10:54.580
I've got the whole place rented out for today.

00:10:54.580 --> 00:10:56.440
May I ask you two questions?

00:10:56.440 --> 00:10:57.440
Go ahead...

00:10:57.440 --> 00:10:59.220
I like a good chat.

00:10:59.370 --> 00:11:01.860
What is your connection with Master Sakaki?

00:11:01.860 --> 00:11:05.020
There was a time when Shio-chan and I were teammates.

00:11:05.180 --> 00:11:06.360
In America that is.

00:11:06.600 --> 00:11:08.340
As bodyguard's to an important person.

00:11:08.340 --> 00:11:09.960
An aide to the FBI.

00:11:10.280 --> 00:11:11.620
Our operation was extensive.

00:11:12.000 --> 00:11:14.580
The drug organizations were obliterated into parts.

00:11:14.580 --> 00:11:17.720
And we were even feared by the police more than the mafia.

00:11:18.340 --> 00:11:20.460
But Shio-chan was just too stubborn.

00:11:20.800 --> 00:11:21.580
Stubborn?

00:11:21.900 --> 00:11:24.680
Because, taking assassination orders was a complete taboo for him...

00:11:24.920 --> 00:11:30.980
He also didn't allow the poor to suffer, the children to cry, and the aged to be harassed.

00:11:31.160 --> 00:11:32.540
What does he think he's doing?

00:11:32.540 --> 00:11:34.360
We're not some charity group you know.

00:11:35.100 --> 00:11:37.580
You should be careful too if you're really his disciple.

00:11:37.580 --> 00:11:38.860
He's a terrible person.

00:11:40.120 --> 00:11:43.180
Once we tried to kill someone using unorthodox methods,

00:11:43.200 --> 00:11:46.380
This won't even do 
as fertilizer.

00:11:43.220 --> 00:11:45.320
he fought back at us and tried to bury us alive in the desert.

00:11:43.790 --> 00:11:46.380
Remember this!

00:11:43.820 --> 00:11:46.380
Why you-

00:11:47.740 --> 00:11:48.480
Then,

00:11:48.630 --> 00:11:52.460
I will ask the next question as a person who is a part of the same martial arts world.

00:11:53.320 --> 00:11:54.160
Go ahead.

00:11:54.480 --> 00:11:57.900
An expert like you, should have something else to aim for.

00:11:58.300 --> 00:12:01.380
But, why did you take the path of an assassin?

00:12:05.360 --> 00:12:07.840
It was a poor French village.

00:12:08.440 --> 00:12:11.880
Where parents gave even their share of food to their kids.

00:12:12.560 --> 00:12:14.930
And the kids who lost their parents,

00:12:15.440 --> 00:12:18.920
eventually had to support their remaining siblings.

00:12:19.940 --> 00:12:22.920
There was no other choice.

00:12:23.640 --> 00:12:26.300
I'm going to take revenge on the world.

00:12:31.160 --> 00:12:33.180
It's still not too late.

00:12:33.180 --> 00:12:35.820
Stop being an assassin and turn over a new leaf!

00:12:38.640 --> 00:12:42.280
That was according to some movie.

00:12:43.200 --> 00:12:44.820
I really cried back there!

00:12:47.400 --> 00:12:48.160
Me?

00:12:48.340 --> 00:12:50.440
Why did I choose to be an assassin?

00:12:50.920 --> 00:12:52.440
Because I love it!

00:12:52.480 --> 00:12:53.660
I love to kill!

00:12:55.620 --> 00:12:57.640
A really bad guy sighted!

00:12:59.180 --> 00:13:01.360
Your master is strong, that is for certain.

00:13:01.360 --> 00:13:03.380
But, he can’t win against me.

00:13:03.520 --> 00:13:04.520
What?

00:13:04.720 --> 00:13:06.020
In battle you see,

00:13:06.100 --> 00:13:08.230
the wittiest one is already victorious.

00:13:09.880 --> 00:13:10.720
Look.

00:13:14.720 --> 00:13:16.280
Master Sakaki!

00:13:16.720 --> 00:13:19.040
He will give in to anything that I say.

00:13:19.040 --> 00:13:23.160
Because his dear disciple is in a dire situation.

00:13:23.720 --> 00:13:26.210
Leave Gauche there and move back.

00:13:29.060 --> 00:13:29.840
Okay.

00:13:29.840 --> 00:13:32.820
Now go straight to the elevator and get out.

00:13:33.030 --> 00:13:34.020
You blockhead.

00:13:37.280 --> 00:13:38.310
See that?

00:13:38.580 --> 00:13:41.840
He'll even give up his client in exchange for the ones he care about.

00:13:42.240 --> 00:13:45.140
Justice is short-lived after all.

00:13:45.140 --> 00:13:46.880
No, you will lose.

00:13:47.080 --> 00:13:47.800
What?

00:13:48.260 --> 00:13:49.720
Against that person.

00:13:53.520 --> 00:13:55.520
Evil is the short-lived thing.

00:14:02.500 --> 00:14:04.860
You seem to have taken good care of my disciple.

00:14:04.860 --> 00:14:07.220
I'll have you accept my gratitude in full!

00:14:07.710 --> 00:14:09.360
Tsk! Fine then.

00:14:09.590 --> 00:14:12.400
But I'll be finishing my job before that.

00:14:12.940 --> 00:14:14.160
Kill Gauche now!

00:14:20.880 --> 00:14:22.440
M-Miu-san!

00:14:23.760 --> 00:14:24.580
What the...?

00:14:24.580 --> 00:14:25.920
I got tricked by Shio!

00:14:26.540 --> 00:14:27.920
Too bad!

00:14:31.420 --> 00:14:33.580
Go back home to hell, Christopher.

00:14:34.000 --> 00:14:36.620
This is not a place for the likes of you!

00:14:37.500 --> 00:14:38.570
My, my.

00:14:38.980 --> 00:14:42.680
But going all out isn't really my style.

00:14:42.820 --> 00:14:43.760
Guess I have no choice.

00:14:43.760 --> 00:14:45.820
Let's settle this, Shio.

00:14:48.840 --> 00:14:51.680
Kenichi-san, move away from there!

00:14:54.880 --> 00:14:57.400
Wait... What are you planning to do?

00:14:59.300 --> 00:15:00.860
I'm coming over there now!

00:15:02.180 --> 00:15:02.900
Now...

00:15:06.100 --> 00:15:07.600
Right now?!

00:15:10.240 --> 00:15:11.900
Where are you looking?

00:15:11.900 --> 00:15:12.840
Behind me?

00:15:16.540 --> 00:15:17.520
Let's do this.

00:15:21.520 --> 00:15:24.820
For them to give my subordinates a hard time like that...

00:15:25.040 --> 00:15:28.500
That girl seems to be more suitable as a disciple.

00:15:28.800 --> 00:15:29.800
You fool.

00:15:29.800 --> 00:15:31.980
That's Fuurinji Hayato's granddaughter.

00:15:32.380 --> 00:15:33.720
Fuurinji Hayato?!

00:15:34.280 --> 00:15:36.600
That's the Invincible Superman's granddaughter?

00:15:36.980 --> 00:15:38.460
Now I see why.

00:15:38.780 --> 00:15:40.910
Then that greenhorn boy is...

00:15:41.760 --> 00:15:44.410
He's the disciple of the entire Ryouzanpaku,

00:15:44.480 --> 00:15:46.300
Shirahama Kenichi!

00:15:46.300 --> 00:15:46.920
What?!

00:15:47.200 --> 00:15:48.810
The entire Ryouzanpaku?!

00:15:49.400 --> 00:15:50.150
That boy?!

00:15:50.940 --> 00:15:51.880
Sharp things are scary.

00:15:51.880 --> 00:15:53.440
Sharp things are scary!

00:15:54.480 --> 00:15:56.440
Rolling Savate is another form of Savate?!

00:15:56.440 --> 00:15:58.460
So it's a part of Savate, huh?!

00:16:00.780 --> 00:16:02.020
That's quite lame.

00:16:02.210 --> 00:16:05.540
I can't understand why you chose him as your disciple.

00:16:06.170 --> 00:16:08.260
Because he's interesting, that's why!

00:16:09.240 --> 00:16:13.040
You might not understand it throughout your whole life though!

00:16:13.980 --> 00:16:16.480
Saying quite suggestive words there I see!

00:16:23.400 --> 00:16:24.960
Oh boy... Wow!

00:16:24.960 --> 00:16:28.080
Honestly their level is so high, I can't even learn from it.

00:16:28.580 --> 00:16:29.120
Look out!

00:16:29.360 --> 00:16:30.040
Scary sharp things.

00:16:30.040 --> 00:16:30.940
Scary sharp things!

00:16:30.940 --> 00:16:31.780
Stop fiddling around!

00:16:36.300 --> 00:16:37.860
What a progressive offense.

00:16:37.860 --> 00:16:38.800
I can’t break through!

00:16:44.640 --> 00:16:45.980
You fight well bitch.

00:16:48.660 --> 00:16:50.200
That was dangerous.

00:16:50.760 --> 00:16:51.860
No good.

00:16:51.860 --> 00:16:54.230
The level here is also too high for me to learn anything...

00:16:55.140 --> 00:16:56.260
Hey, hey.

00:16:56.480 --> 00:16:58.720
He's really some useless disciple.

00:17:01.000 --> 00:17:03.400
He just an average guy no matter how I look at it after all.

00:17:03.880 --> 00:17:05.820
A disciple with weak powers of observation!

00:17:06.480 --> 00:17:08.160
Just shut up and fight!

00:17:08.840 --> 00:17:09.680
Don’t move!

00:17:11.240 --> 00:17:12.340
What is that?

00:17:12.600 --> 00:17:16.140
I-I, Wynn Gauche the great weapons merchant,

00:17:16.320 --> 00:17:19.840
